# test/capdisclose.map -- CAP-DISCLOSE-LINT (B43): how each answer-path cap constant discloses that it fired.
# Read by test/lib/capdisclose.py (its docstring is the contract); gated by test/capdisclosemapcheck.sh.
# Columns (TAB-separated): kName  CLASS  [awaits:#N]
#   sink:a,b        every function with a cap site of kName mentions a or b -- removing that disclosure reds the gate
#   legend          a static_assert ties kName to the legend sentence that states the cap
#   none:<reason>   not an answer cut
#   pending:<id> r  a cut whose function names no disclosure identifier: baselined, printed as INFO, to audit
#   awaits:#N       the constant is on an unmerged lane (absent = INFO, present = checked)
# How the rows were made (2026-11-12): `capdisclose.py . /dev/null --draft` proposed every row from the identifiers present
# at EVERY cap site's function (capped / more / cut / shown / floor / truncated / DISCLOSE ...). A sink row therefore holds
# the disclosure that is there today in place; it does not prove that identifier reports THIS cap -- a reviewer who reads a
# function and finds otherwise reclassifies the row to pending. #614's depth cap and #613's reader cap are the two rows read
# by hand (CodeRabbit 4542271958 and 4540061421): both lanes' red revisions FAIL their row and the fixed revisions PASS.
# A new cap constant on the answer path needs a row here in the same commit.
kAnswerPageBytesDefault	none:the default page stop the answer-first ORDER rules read (AF2 G, KB1 insertKeyBodies: a key body is added only when the answer block ends inside it): a block moves or is added, every row is still emitted once (answerFirst's size ENSURES; forkeybodycheck K3n); the page cut itself is disclosed by page= pages= withheld_bytes= next= (forpages.h)
kBlockBytes	legend
kImportSpecDepth	sink:atDepthCap
kMaxSitesPerTok	legend
kRareWordSites	legend
kReaderCallerReaders	sink:readersMore
kAliasHopChains	sink:cut,shown
kAliasHopMemberNames	sink:cut,shown
kAliasHopSigBytes	sink:cut,truncateUtf8WithEllipsis
kCMakeMaxCallLines	pending:#565 a read bound on one CMake call: past 16 lines the call still names its target (its first argument), but an IMPORTED / ALIAS keyword there is unseen and the row prints; stated in docs/LIMITS.md, no attribute says it fired
kCallPathSeeds	none:K4 keep-guard seed window: which seeds the guard tries, no answer row is cut (LARGE-PARTIAL Stage 0 audit)
kCloneKeyTokenBits	none:a saturating key field width, re-verified: a wider key changes no row (Stage 0 audit)
kDeadExportedRowsShown	sink:shown,walkSkipped
kDispatchArmMaxRows	none:a tangle shape test, not a cut: a dispatch arm of at most 40 lines reads alone, so its depth is exempt from the score; no row or answer is cut (QD-TANGLE, train ge2)
kEvidenceCap	pending:B43 disclosed elsewhere: pageTailOf emits shown= capped= for every pageWindow (verbs_navigate.h); the cap is used through a window, so the lint finds no cap site to tie
kForBareFlagMaxSites	none:a shape test, not a cut: a bare kebab token with more source sites is prose, so no <lit shape="flag"> is claimed (WHOLE-TOKEN; read by hand at train 1111c)
kForBodyFoldBudgetBytes	sink:cut,firstCutNext
kForBodyFoldRows	none:the scope of an additive fold: rows past it are printed unfolded, none dropped (Stage 0 audit)
kForBodySlotMaxBytes	legend
kForBudgetRowFloor	none:a keep floor, not a cut: the best-ranked <sigs> rows it keeps are never shed; an answer still over --token-budget at the floor prices more than the budget names (est_tokens= above it), and --max-tokens says over_ceiling= (TOKEN-BUDGET-MONOTONE; read by hand at train 1111i)
